lb-9lnz.description:
Add optional TuiSender field to Logger and new methods:

  pub struct Logger {
      writer: SharedWriter,
      tui: Option<TuiSender>,  // new
  }

  impl Logger {
      // existing new() unchanged (tui: None)
      pub fn with_tui(path: &Path, tui: TuiSender) -> io::Result<Self>
      pub fn with_label(&self, label: &str) -> Self  // clone with different pane label, shared file writer

      // Modified:
      pub fn log(&self, msg: &str)  // → TUI if present, else eprintln!; always writes to file
      pub fn display(&self, msg: &str)  // → TUI if present, else println!; does NOT write to file
      pub fn tee_stderr(&self, ...)  // drain to TUI if present, else eprintln!; always writes to file
      pub fn tee_stdout(&self, ...)  // same pattern
  }

  impl TuiSender {
      pub fn with_label(&self, label: &str) -> Self  // clone with new pane label, same tx
  }

The with_label() method on Logger creates a clone that shares the same file writer (Arc<Mutex<...>>) but routes to a different TUI pane. Used for concurrent summary/decider stages.

lb-eivs.description:
Changes to loop_cmd::execute():

1. Add tui: Option<&TuiHandle> parameter. Forward to run::execute().

2. For the concurrent summary+decider thread::scope block, create per-stage loggers using Logger::with_label():
   let summary_logger = logger_opt.as_ref().map(|l| l.with_label("SUMMARY"));
   let decider_logger = logger_opt.as_ref().map(|l| l.with_label("DECISION"));
   // Pass summary_logger to summary::execute(), decider_logger to should_continue()

3. For reviewer:
   let reviewer_logger = logger_opt.as_ref().map(|l| l.with_label("CODE REVIEW"));
   // Pass to reviewer::execute()

This causes summary, decider, and reviewer to each appear in their own TUI pane while sharing the same log file.

Note: Bare eprintln! calls in loop_cmd.rs (bootstrap, branch setup banners) can stay as-is for v1 — they go to the hidden main screen in alternate-screen mode. They are already logged to file via Logger.

lb-okra.description:
Changes to run::execute():

1. Add tui: Option<&TuiHandle> parameter.

2. Logger construction:
   let logger = match tui {
       Some(t) => Logger::with_tui(&log_path, t.sender("AGENT SESSION"))?,
       None => Logger::new(&log_path)?,
   };

3. In the stream_output closure, replace println!("{formatted}") with logger.display(&formatted):
   handle.stream_output(|line| {
       let _ = writeln!(jsonl_writer, "{line}");
       if let Some(formatted) = stream_fmt::format_line(&mut formatter, line) {
           logger.display(&formatted);   // → TUI or stdout
           logger.log_file_only(&formatted);
       }
   })

4. For raw mode (opts.raw), similarly replace println!("{line}") with logger.display(line).

5. Return logger so loop_cmd can use it for subsequent stages (existing behavior).

lb-yzzv.description:
Currently decider uses --output-format json --json-schema ...; its reasoning is invisible.

Changes in should_continue():
1. Keep --json-schema (it constrains agent output to valid JSON per schema; works with stream-json).
2. Change --output-format from json to stream-json.
3. Replace manual wait_with_output() + tee_stderr with run_streaming_claude(child, &mut formatter, logger).
4. Parse structured output from the returned result string instead of parsed["structured_output"]:
   let result_json: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&result_text)?;
   let action = result_json["action"].as_str()...;
   let reason = result_json["reason"].as_str()...;

Result: DECISION pane shows the decider's reasoning, what it reads (SPEC.md, lb ready), and the final decision — fully visible.
